# Git

All work in this project happens under git. One repository per app — don't make the whole
workspace a single repo.

- **Before editing**: check the target is a repository (`git -C <dir> status`). If it isn't,
  `git init` and make an initial commit before touching anything. If there are uncommitted
  changes already, ask before mixing your own work in.
- **After editing**: commit at each working checkpoint. Don't wait to be asked. One commit per
  change, with a message that says what changed.
- **Never create `.bak` files.** Commit instead — that's what git is for. No
  `index.html.bak-<label>-<date>` style backups.
- **New tool**: create `apps/<tool-name>/` and **`git init` before writing anything**.
- **`.gitignore`**: exclude `node_modules`, build and test output, regenerable large assets
  (track the generator, ignore the output), `.DS_Store`, and credentials (`*.env`).
  - ⚠ A trailing slash (`tests/node_modules/`) **matches directories only and lets symlinks
    through**. Drop the slash where a symlink is possible.

